          "date": "2025-10-18T09:25:30Z",
          "language": "en",
          "section": "us_news",
          "raw_content": "Bézier curves are a core building block of text and 2D shapes rendering. There are several approaches to rendering them, but one especially challenging problem, both mathematically and technically, is computing the distance to a Bézier curve. For quadratic curves (one control point), this is fairly accessible, but for cubic (two control points) we're going to see why it is so hard. Having this distance field opens up many rendering possibilities. It's hard, but it's possible; here is a live proof:",
